# Keep local development state out of the image.
#
# The immediate reason: .env.local is a developer's machine-local override, but
# `COPY . .` copied it into the build, where `npm run build` inlined its
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* values into the client bundle. A wrong value there is not a
# runtime setting you can correct by restarting the container — it is compiled
# into the JavaScript the browser downloads, so it survives until the next
# rebuild. Configure the container through compose `environment` instead.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

node_modules
.next
npm-debug.log*

.git
.github
.vscode
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
README.md
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
.agents
.heroui-docs
